# Files and directories excluded from the built plugin zip (wp dist-archive).
# Development, branding, and wordpress.org listing assets.
#
# What is left behind is the plugin plus LICENSE, readme.txt, and two files kept
# deliberately: CONTRIBUTING.md and SECURITY.md. SECURITY.md is how someone who
# found a hole in an installed copy learns where to report it privately, and a
# reporter who has only the zip has nowhere else to look. That is worth the two
# files. Everything else here is noise inside wp-content/plugins.
/.git
/.github
/.claude
/bin
/.wordpress-org
/branding
/playground
/tests
/vendor
/node_modules
/.gitignore
/.distignore
/composer.json
/composer.lock
/phpcs.xml
/phpcompat.xml
#
# The build's own output directory. bin/build-zip.sh excludes the directory it
# is writing to, but only that one: build into `dist` while a `build/` from an
# earlier run is still sitting there and the old package ships inside the new
# one. This is the entry that covers the leftover.
/build
#
# Compiled translations. The .pot stays — it is what translate.wordpress.org
# and any downstream translator start from — but the per-locale catalogs do
# not ship. wordpress.org generates and delivers those for every locale from
# the strings in the code, so a bundled copy is a second source for the same
# translation that can only drift from the one users actually receive.
/languages/*.po
/languages/*.mo
/README.md
/ROADMAP.md
/TODO.md
/docs
